{
  "name": "std-agent-tool-loop",
  "description": "std-agent-tool-loop — answers a conversation by operating the running app as the caller, through `call-service llm call-tools`. The `tools` allowlist names declared external inputs (addressed like a listens source: `Trait.EVENT`, `Orbital.Trait.EVENT`) and entities to read; each input fires as the signed-in user through the ordinary dispatch (guards and entity policies apply) and each read returns only the rows the caller may read. Headless: the conversation UI (std-agent-session) shows the reply; a failure shows as a toast. CONVERSE carries the conversation (and optionally what std-agent-memory recalled); REPLIED carries the reply, every tool step and the token usage; REPLY_FAILED carries the error. Compose with std-agent-session (the conversation) and std-agent-trace (the step record).",
