  "source": "",
  "lolo": "app std-agent-tool-loop \"2.0.0\"\n\"std-agent-tool-loop — answers a conversation by operating the running app as the caller, through `call-service llm call-tools`. The `tools` allowlist names declared external inputs (addressed like a listens source: `Trait.EVENT`, `Orbital.Trait.EVENT`) and entities to read; each input fires as the signed-in user through the ordinary dispatch (guards and entity policies apply) and each read returns only the rows the caller may read. Headless: the conversation UI (std-agent-session) shows the reply; a failure shows as a toast. CONVERSE carries the conversation (and optionally what std-agent-memory recalled); REPLIED carries the reply, every tool step and the token usage; REPLY_FAILED carries the error. Compose with std-agent-session (the conversation) and std-agent-trace (the step record).\"\n\ntype AgentTool = {\n  event : event\n  read : string\n}\ntype AgentChatMessage = {\n  role : \"user\" | \"assistant\"\n  content : string!\n}\ntype AgentStep = {\n  kind : \"input\" | \"read\" | \"invalid\"\n  target : string!\n  args : string!\n  ok : boolean!\n  detail : string\n}\ntype AgentUsage = {\n  promptTokens : number!\n  completionTokens : number!\n  totalTokens : number!\n  modelCalls : number!\n}\n\norbital AgentToolLoopOrbital {\n  entity AgentTurn [runtime] {\n    id : string!\n    status : \"idle\" | \"thinking\" | \"answered\" | \"failed\" @description \"Where the current turn is.\" = idle\n    reply : string @description \"The last reply.\" = \"\"\n    error : string @description \"Why the last turn failed.\" = \"\"\n  }\n\n  trait AgentToolLoop -> AgentTurn [interaction] {\n    config {\n      tools : [AgentTool] = []\n        @label \"What may the assistant do?\"\n        @description \"The declared inputs it may fire (`{ event: Trait.EVENT }`) and the entities it may read (`{ read: Entity }`), as the signed-in user.\"\n        @synonyms \"allowlist, abilities, actions, permissions\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      instructions : string = \"You operate this app for the signed-in user. Use the tools to act and to look things up; when a tool reports that something was refused or denied, say so plainly.\"\n        @label \"How should the assistant behave?\"\n        @description \"Standing instructions sent with every conversation.\"\n        @synonyms \"system prompt, persona, guidance\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      maxSteps : number = 8\n        @label \"Model round-trips per request\"\n        @description \"How many model calls one request may take before it fails.\"\n        @tier \"policy\"\n    }\n    initial: idle\n\n    state idle {\n      INIT -> idle\n        (set @entity.status idle)\n      CONVERSE -> thinking\n        (set @entity.status thinking)\n        (call-service llm call-tools {\n          messages: ?messages\n          tools: @config.tools\n          instructions: (if [\"=\", (str/default ?context \"\"), \"\"] @config.instructions (str/concat @config.instructions \"\\n\\nWhat you remember that may be relevant:\\n\" ?context))\n          maxSteps: @config.maxSteps\n        } {\n          emit: { failure: ASK_FAILED, success: ANSWERED }\n        })\n    }\n\n    state thinking {\n      ANSWERED -> idle\n        (set @entity.status answered)\n        (set @entity.reply ?reply)\n        (emit REPLIED { reply: ?reply, steps: ?steps, usage: ?usage })\n      ASK_FAILED -> idle\n        (set @entity.status failed)\n        (set @entity.error ?error)\n        (emit REPLY_FAILED { error: ?error })\n        (render-ui toast {\n          message: ?error\n          type: alert\n          variant: error\n        })\n    }\n\n    emits {\n      REPLIED -> external {\n        reply : string!\n        steps : [AgentStep]!\n        usage : AgentUsage!\n      }\n        @description \"The assistant answered; carries every tool step it took and the tokens it used.\"\n        @synonyms \"answered, responded, done\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      REPLY_FAILED -> external {\n        error : string!\n      }\n        @description \"The assistant could not answer (model unavailable, or out of steps).\"\n        @synonyms \"failed, error, gave up\"\n        @tier \"domain\"\n      ANSWERED -> internal {\n        reply : string!\n        steps : [AgentStep]!\n        usage : AgentUsage!\n      }\n        @tier \"internal\"\n      ASK_FAILED -> internal {\n        error : string!\n      }\n        @tier \"internal\"\n    }\n\n    listens {\n      CONVERSE {\n        messages : [AgentChatMessage]!\n        context : string\n      }\n        @description \"Answer this conversation; the last turn is the request. `context` is what the assistant remembers that may be relevant.\"\n        @synonyms \"ask, chat, request\"\n    }\n  }\n\n  page \"/agent-tool-loop\" as AgentToolLoopPage -> AgentToolLoop\n}\n"
}